From scheduler interactive session 2026-07-27, /cloture step 2+3. Two items realisateur owns, filed through the front door because check-project-busy reported BUSY (live session pid 462531) so a direct write was deferred. (1) DOCTRINE PROPOSAL -- BUILD-DISCIPLINE.md failure pattern 16, "a correct refusal that nothing retries": a guard declines to act, is RIGHT to decline, logs loudly, and nothing ever revisits the decision, so the refusal is permanent by omission. Distinct from pattern 8 (warn-then-continue PROCEEDS; this one correctly STOPS and the stopping is the loss) and from 13 (that is a decision with no dispatch path; this is finished WORK with none). Live exhibits, all from one session: scheduler-dev-cycle.sh dirty-tree merge fallback and its failed-push path stranded 14 commits across 2026-07-25/26, each logging loudly every time -- which is why this deserves doctrine: "it failed loud" turned out NOT to be sufficient, the missing property is a named retry. Rule shape: a fallback that declines to act must name what retries it, or it is a dead end wearing a safe fallback clothes. Fixed in scheduler by reconcile_prior_cycles() (dd086bb). (2) RECORD GAP: realisateur .scheduler/FOCUS.md has no entry for c49c70d (session-marker.sh: record a pid that outlives the hook, pushed 2026-07-27) -- that repo currently carries a commit its own nightly cannot explain. Both were first filed in scheduler FOCUS.md, which was WRONG and is itself an instance of pattern 13: scheduler dev-cycle is hard-barred from touching any file outside its own repo (bin/scheduler-dev-cycle.sh:282,284) and realisateur nightly-batch.md explicitly says not to act on other projects FOCUS items unprompted, so nothing that could act on them would ever read them.
